@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Constraints Introduction";
}

<section>

    <!-- =====================================================
         PAGE INTRODUCTION
         ===================================================== -->

    <div class="mb-5">

        <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Constraints Introduction
        </h1>

        <p class="lead text-muted">
            SQL Server constraints are rules applied to table columns
            to maintain data accuracy, consistency and integrity.
            Constraints help control what type of data can be inserted
            or stored in a table.
        </p>

    </div>


    <!-- =====================================================
         WHAT ARE CONSTRAINTS?
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            What are Constraints?
        </h2>

        <p>
            A constraint is a rule that is applied to a column or
            table to control the data that can be stored.
        </p>

        <p>
            Constraints help ensure that invalid or unwanted data
            is not inserted into the database.
        </p>

        <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

            <h5 class="fw-bold">
                Simple Example
            </h5>

            <p class="mb-0">
                If every student must have a unique StudentId,
                we can use a <strong>PRIMARY KEY</strong> constraint
                to enforce that rule.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         WHY CONSTRAINTS?
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Why Do We Need Constraints?
        </h2>

        <p>
            Constraints help maintain the quality and integrity of
            data stored in database tables.
        </p>

        <ul>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Prevent invalid data.
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Maintain data integrity.
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Prevent duplicate values where required.
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Establish relationships between tables.
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Apply rules to column values.
            </li>

            <li>
                Provide consistency across the database.
            </li>

        </ul>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         TYPES OF CONSTRAINTS
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Types of SQL Server Constraints
        </h2>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>Constraint</th>
                        <th>Purpose</th>
                        <th>Example</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>PRIMARY KEY</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Uniquely identifies each record in a table.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            StudentId
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>FOREIGN KEY</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Creates a relationship between tables.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            CourseId
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>UNIQUE</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Prevents duplicate values in a column.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Email
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>NOT NULL</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Prevents NULL values in a column.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            StudentName
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>DEFAULT</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Provides a default value when no value is supplied.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Status
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>CHECK</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Restricts values according to a condition.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Age &gt;= 18
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         CONSTRAINT STRUCTURE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Constraint Structure
        </h2>

        <p>
            Constraints can be applied while creating a table or
            added later to an existing table.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL Server
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>
                                                                Database
                                                                   ↓
                                                                 Table
                                                                   ↓
                                                                Columns
                                                                   ↓
                                                                Constraints
                                                                   ↓
                                                                Data Integrity</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         SIMPLE EXAMPLE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Constraints Example
        </h2>

        <p>
            The following example uses multiple constraints while
            creating a Students table.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE TABLE Students
(
    StudentId INT PRIMARY KEY,

    StudentName VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,

    Email VARCHAR(150) UNIQUE,

    Age INT CHECK (Age >= 18),

    Status VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'Active'
);</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         OUTPUT / STRUCTURE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Example Table Structure
        </h2>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>Column</th>
                        <th>Data Type</th>
                        <th>Constraint</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            StudentId
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            INT
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            PRIMARY KEY
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            StudentName
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            VARCHAR(100)
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            NOT NULL
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            Email
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            VARCHAR(150)
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            UNIQUE
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            Age
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            INT
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            CHECK
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            Status
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            VARCHAR(20)
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            DEFAULT
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         DATA INTEGRITY
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Constraints and Data Integrity
        </h2>

        <p>
            Data integrity means maintaining accurate and consistent
            data in the database.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL Server
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>Valid Data
    ↓
Constraints
    ↓
Database Rules
    ↓
Accurate & Consistent Data</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         IMPORTANT POINTS
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <div class="alert alert-info border-0">

            <h5 class="fw-bold">
                Important Points
            </h5>

            <ul class="mb-0">

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Constraints enforce rules on table data.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Different constraints solve different data
                    integrity requirements.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Constraints can be defined during table creation.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Constraints can also be added to existing tables.
                </li>

            </ul>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         SUMMARY
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-4">

        <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Summary
            </h2>

            <p class="mb-0">
                In this section, we learned what SQL Server constraints
                are, why they are required and the different types of
                constraints used to maintain data integrity.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


